## Why This Is Asked
Tests familiarity with MVVM, Room, Retrofit, and offline-first UX. Focus on data flow, error handling, and testability.

## Key Concepts
- Room: Entity, DAO, migrations
- Retrofit: API interface, suspend functions
- MVVM: ViewModel + LiveData
- Offline-first: Cache-first, background sync

## Code Example
```kotlin
@Entity
data class Article(
  @PrimaryKey val id: String,
  val title: String,
  val body: String?,
  val updatedAt: Long
)

@Dao
interface ArticleDao {
  @Query("SELECT * FROM Article ORDER BY updatedAt DESC")
  fun getAll(): LiveData<List<Article>>

  @Insert(onConflict = OnConflictStrategy.REPLACE)
  suspend fun insertAll(articles: List<Article>)
}

interface ArticleApi {
  @GET("articles")
  suspend fun getArticles(): List<Article>
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the offline-first behavior and ensure data consistency across offline/online states?
- What simple metrics would you collect to validate user-perceived freshness without overfetching?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates IPC design and dynamic, sandboxed plugin loading in a production Android application. It tests understanding of cross-process boundaries, lifecycle management, and secure plugin distribution.

## Key Concepts
- Android isolated processes and AIDL
- Runtime DEX/plugin loading with security guarantees
- Android Keystore attestation for plugin signatures
- Per-plugin resource quotas and storage isolation
- Live feature or module swapping with rollback

## Code Example
```java
// AIDL surface sketch
aidl interface IThemeProvider {
    Palette getPalette();
    Typography getTypography();
    Shape getShape();
}

// Host ProcessManager
aidlassealed class ThemePluginHost {
    private val plugins = ConcurrentHashMap<String, IBinder>()

    fun bindPlugin(pluginId: String, intent: Intent) {
        val connection = object : ServiceConnection {
            override fun onServiceConnected(name: ComponentName?, service: IBinder?) {
                plugins[pluginId] = service
            }
            override fun onServiceDisconnected(name: ComponentName?) {
                plugins.remove(pluginId)
            }
        }
        bindService(intent, connection, Context.BIND_AUTO_CREATE)
    }

    fun applyTheme(pluginId: String, theme: Theme) {
        val provider = IThemeProvider.Stub.asInterface(plugins[pluginId])
        val palette = provider.getPalette()
        // Apply to host UI
    }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests knowledge of Android dynamic feature modules, remote config gating, and safe in-app upgrades with rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Dynamic Feature Modules and SplitInstallManager
- Remote Config feature flags and gating
- Module metadata and compatibility checks
- Data migrations scoped to features
- Rollback strategies and robust test plans

## Code Example
```javascript
// Module metadata and compatibility check (illustrative)
class ModuleMeta { constructor(name, version, minAppVersion, minApi) {
  this.name = name; this.version = version; this.minAppVersion = minAppVersion; this.minApi = minApi;
}}
function isCompatible(meta, appVersion, deviceApi) {
  return appVersion >= meta.minAppVersion && deviceApi >= meta.minApi;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test upgrades across multiple device configurations and network conditions?
- How would you handle partial upgrades when device storage or network is constrained?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-process, low-latency audio paths on Android, including security and performance.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time audio path with AAudio
- Cross-process IPC via AIDL
- android:process and android:isolatedProcess
- Shared memory (ashmem) for zero-copy buffers
- Remote config for per-user audio chains; Keystore encryption
- Performance tests: latency, jitter, power

